# Provider API Version Manifest

CODEX: [02-data/provider-api-version-manifest.md](../../unified-trading-codex/02-data/provider-api-version-manifest.md)

---

## Rule summary

Every external provider schema module (`unified_api_contracts_external/{provider}/*.py`)
must carry a **module-level `__api_version__` constant** matching the `api_version`
entry in `provider_api_versions.yaml`.

```python
# DO — at the top of each schema file (after the module docstring)
__api_version__ = "v3"  # matches provider_api_versions.yaml
```

```python
# NEVER — omit the constant or use a different version than the YAML
```

---

## DO

- Keep `provider_api_versions.yaml` updated whenever a provider releases a new version
- Set `status: yellow` after bumping `api_version` until cassettes are re-recorded
- Set `status: green` only after schema validation tests pass against live/cassette data
- Update `last_verified` to today's ISO date when re-recording cassettes
- Run `python3 scripts/generate_schema_version_matrix.py` after any YAML change

## NEVER

- Set `status: red` except to signal a real breaking change (STEP 5.17 will fail CI)
- Let `__api_version__` in a schema file differ from `api_version` in the YAML — this auto-computes `red`
- Add a provider schema directory without a corresponding entry in the YAML
- Hard-code the version string in `__api_version__` to something other than what the live API uses

---

## Status definitions (quick ref)

| Status | Meaning | CI impact |
|--------|---------|-----------|
| `green` | Verified < 90 days | None |
| `yellow` | Unverified or > 90 days | Warn only |
| `red` | Breaking change / mismatch | **STEP 5.17 fails** |

